# Coding guidelines

## UI: Tailwind + shadcn

Build UI with the existing Tailwind + shadcn (new-york) setup. Prefer primitives from `@/components/ui` and add missing ones with `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>`.

Never invent a custom component when shadcn already provides it (Button, Dialog, Select, Table, Tabs, Form, etc.). Compose and style with Tailwind; do not hand-roll equivalents.

## YAGNI and one-liners

Ship only what the current task needs. No speculative abstractions, wrappers, or config.

Prefer a clear one-liner over a multi-step ceremony when the intent stays obvious.

```tsx
// ✅
const label = status === "live" ? "Live" : "Idle";

// ❌
function getStatusLabel(status: string) {
  if (status === "live") return "Live";
  return "Idle";
}
```

## Comments

Keep comments rare. Names and structure should carry meaning.

If a block needs multiple lines of comments to be understood, that code is invalid. Decompose it into smaller pieces or rethink the design until it reads without a essay.

```ts
// ✅ rare, short, non-obvious why
// Bustabit WS sends bust as integer cents

// ❌ narrating what the code already says
// Loop through games and filter the ones that busted
```
